        <mxCell id="backToPool" value="↲  back into the pool for another courier" style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=11;fontColor=#475569;fontColor=#9a3412;fontStyle=1;fontSize=12;align=center;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="370" y="898" width="340" height="24" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="noteWhy" value="Why it takes two parties

A courier pressing &quot;collected&quot; is only their word for it. Until the shop confirms, nobody has actually taken the parcel — so it is not treated as collected, and the customer is given nobody’s number.

This is the project’s answer to the problem statement: logistics &quot;organized manually between sellers and courier services&quot;." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=16;fillColor=#eef2ff;strokeColor=#4f46e5;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=4;fontSize=11;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#4338ca;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1410" y="240" width="340" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="noteRace" value="Two couriers cannot both win

Claiming is a single conditional UPDATE. The second courier changes no rows and is told somebody got there first, so nobody travels for a parcel that is gone." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=16;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#b45309;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=4;fontSize=11;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#78350f;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1410" y="460" width="340" height="130" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="noteException" value="One exception to the gating

The shop being asked to confirm sees the courier’s name from the moment they ask — it is being asked to verify that this person took the parcel, which it cannot do against an anonymous claim." style="shape=note;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;size=16;fillColor=#fffbeb;strokeColor=#b45309;align=left;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=4;fontSize=11;verticalAlign=top;fontColor=#78350f;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="1410" y="620" width="340" height="150" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
